Sam walks on a 2×2 grid of squares labeled as follows:
\begin{tabular}[t]{|c|c|}\hline 1&2\\ \hline 4&3 \\ \hline \end{tabular}
Two squares are adjacent if they share a side. He starts at the square labeled 1 and every second walks to an adjacent square. How many paths can Sam take so that the sum of the numbers on every square he visits in his path is equal to 20 (not counting the square he started on)?

What percent of square $EFGH$ is shaded? All angles in the diagram are right angles. [asy]
import graph;
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7));

xaxis(0,6,Ticks(1.0,NoZero));
yaxis(0,6,Ticks(1.0,NoZero));

fill((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle);
fill((3,0)--(4,0)--(4,4)--(0,4)--(0,3)--(3,3)--cycle);
fill((5,0)--(6,0)--(6,6)--(0,6)--(0,5)--(5,5)--cycle);

label("$E$",(0,0),SW);
label("$F$",(0,6),N);
label("$G$",(6,6),NE);
label("$H$",(6,0),E);[/asy]

